## Lenso UI — MIT

- Repository: https://github.com/LioRael/lenso-ui
- Files read: `packages/tokens/themes/default/materials.css`,
  `packages/tokens/src/tokens.stylex.const.ts`, `packages/glass/README.md`,
  `DESIGN.md`
- License: MIT
- Used for: the structure of the material design tokens (`tokens::materials`:
  a fill per appearance plus a blur radius, near-translucent fills for
  `ultra-thin`/`thin`, an opaque-enough `thick` for text, a `chrome` bar, and
  more opaque fills in increased contrast), the blur distances (20–30 pt), and
  the rule that glass belongs to the floating layer only. No CSS was copied: the
  values are nsh-cupertino's own tokens, generated from `src/tokens.rs`.

